{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q7449457","formula":"C₂₄H₁₅NO₄","hill":"C24H15NO4","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":24.0,"H":15.0,"N":1.0,"O":4.0},"names":{"en":"Seminaphtharhodafluor"},"descriptions":{"en":"Seminaphtharhodafluor or SNARF is a fluorescent dye that changes color with pH. It can be used to construct optical biosensors that use enzymes that change pH. The absorption peak of the derivative carboxy-SNARF at pH 6.0 is at wavelength (515 and) 550 nm, while that at pH 9.0 is at 575 nm. The emission peak of carboxy-SNARF at pH 6.0 is at wavelength 585 nm, while that at pH 9.0 is at 640 nm. SNARF-1 can serve as a substrate for the MRP1 (multidrug resistance-associated protein-1) drug transporter, to measure the activity of the MRP1 transporter."},"fame":4,"pubchemCid":71308270,"mass":381.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1=CC=C2C(=C1)C(=O)OC23C4=C(C=C(C=C4)N)OC5=C3C=CC6=C5C=CC(=C6)O","inchikey":"DYPYMMHZGRPOCK-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"10'-amino-3'-hydroxyspiro[2-benzofuran-3,7'-benzo[c]xanthene]-1-one","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"71308270","atoms":44,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-3.781,"y":-2.745,"z":1.32,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.849,"y":-1.994,"z":2.056,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.93,"y":-1.161,"z":1.408,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.962,"y":-1.096,"z":0.022,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.884,"y":-1.839,"z":-0.686,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.805,"y":-2.671,"z":-0.073,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.702,"y":-1.587,"z":-2.107,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.345,"y":-2.077,"z":-3.013,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.674,"y":-0.699,"z":-2.228,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.123,"y":-0.311,"z":-0.939,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.299,"y":1.184,"z":-0.772,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.282,"y":1.917,"z":-0.161,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.426,"y":3.288,"z":0.075,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.568,"y":3.968,"z":-0.349,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.608,"y":3.232,"z":-0.916,"el":"C"},{"x